[2026-06-15 23:45:15] [INFO] [PreToolUse] Input: {"session_id":"96f63f83-8d76-415f-b37f-2863ccc07e73","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\EDY\\.claude\\projects\\D--development-code-claude-hk\\96f63f83-8d76-415f-b37f-2863ccc07e73.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\development\\code\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Claude Code env vars for model routing","prompt":"I need an accurate, current list of Claude Code (the CLI) environment variables that control MODEL ROUTING and behavior — specifically the ones that let a user point different \"roles\" of the model (main conversation, background small/fast model, subagents, and the default opus/sonnet/haiku aliases) at different model IDs.\n\nFor each variable, give: exact env var name, what it controls, and how it interacts with the others (precedence/overrides). Specifically cover at least these and confirm whether they exist and are still current:\n- ANTHROPIC_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL\n- CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL\n\nAlso include any OTHER relevant env vars that affect which model is selected for a given task (e.g. model override for specific roles, fast mode, anything that maps an alias like \"opus\"/\"sonnet\"/\"haiku\" to a concrete model ID).\n\nContext: this is for building a reverse proxy (claude-tap-plus) that injects env into the Claude Code subprocess to route by model. The proxy rewrites the request `model` field per-alias, so the user needs to know exactly which env vars to set so that each \"role\" in Claude Code sends a distinct model name that the proxy can then route. Note also that ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL is force-set by the proxy, so that one is out of scope.\n\nPlease verify against current official docs (docs.claude.com / docs.anthropic.com Claude Code settings or environment variables page). Return a concise authoritative table I can hand to the user.","subagent_type":"claude-code-guide"},"tool_use_id":"call_4c70c0a1c7a74a9b93202fff"}
