[2026-06-15 23:45:51] [INFO] [PostToolUse] Input: {"session_id":"96f63f83-8d76-415f-b37f-2863ccc07e73","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\EDY\\.claude\\projects\\D--development-code-claude-hk\\96f63f83-8d76-415f-b37f-2863ccc07e73.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\development\\code\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Claude Code env vars for model routing","prompt":"I need an accurate, current list of Claude Code (the CLI) environment variables that control MODEL ROUTING and behavior — specifically the ones that let a user point different \"roles\" of the model (main conversation, background small/fast model, subagents, and the default opus/sonnet/haiku aliases) at different model IDs.\n\nFor each variable, give: exact env var name, what it controls, and how it interacts with the others (precedence/overrides). Specifically cover at least these and confirm whether they exist and are still current:\n- ANTHROPIC_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL\n- CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL\n\nAlso include any OTHER relevant env vars that affect which model is selected for a given task (e.g. model override for specific roles, fast mode, anything that maps an alias like \"opus\"/\"sonnet\"/\"haiku\" to a concrete model ID).\n\nContext: this is for building a reverse proxy (claude-tap-plus) that injects env into the Claude Code subprocess to route by model. The proxy rewrites the request `model` field per-alias, so the user needs to know exactly which env vars to set so that each \"role\" in Claude Code sends a distinct model name that the proxy can then route. Note also that ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL is force-set by the proxy, so that one is out of scope.\n\nPlease verify against current official docs (docs.claude.com / docs.anthropic.com Claude Code settings or environment variables page). Return a concise authoritative table I can hand to the user.","subagent_type":"claude-code-guide"},"tool_response":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need an accurate, current list of Claude Code (the CLI) environment variables that control MODEL ROUTING and behavior — specifically the ones that let a user point different \"roles\" of the model (main conversation, background small/fast model, subagents, and the default opus/sonnet/haiku aliases) at different model IDs.\n\nFor each variable, give: exact env var name, what it controls, and how it interacts with the others (precedence/overrides). Specifically cover at least these and confirm whether they exist and are still current:\n- ANTHROPIC_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL\n- ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL\n- CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL\n\nAlso include any OTHER relevant env vars that affect which model is selected for a given task (e.g. model override for specific roles, fast mode, anything that maps an alias like \"opus\"/\"sonnet\"/\"haiku\" to a concrete model ID).\n\nContext: this is for building a reverse proxy (claude-tap-plus) that injects env into the Claude Code subprocess to route by model. The proxy rewrites the request `model` field per-alias, so the user needs to know exactly which env vars to set so that each \"role\" in Claude Code sends a distinct model name that the proxy can then route. Note also that ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL is force-set by the proxy, so that one is out of scope.\n\nPlease verify against current official docs (docs.claude.com / docs.anthropic.com Claude Code settings or environment variables page). Return a concise authoritative table I can hand to the user.","agentId":"a0553b2a8a9f275f6","agentType":"claude-code-guide","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the official Claude Code documentation, here's an authoritative table of environment variables that control MODEL ROUTING and behavior:\n\n## Claude Code Model Routing Environment Variables\n\n### Primary Model Selection\n\n| Variable | Purpose | Notes |\n|----------|---------|-------|\n| `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` | Sets the model alias (e.g., `sonnet`, `opus`, `haiku`, `fable`) or full model ID for the main conversation | Overridden by `--model` flag and `/model` command. Takes precedence over `model` setting in settings.json |\n| `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL` | Sets the model for all subagents and agent teams | Overrides per-invocation `model` parameter and subagent definition's `model` frontmatter. Set to `inherit` to use normal model resolution |\n\n### Model Alias Resolution (maps aliases to concrete model IDs)\n\n| Variable | Purpose | Notes |\n|----------|---------|-------|\n| `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL` | Model ID for `opus` alias and `opusplan` in plan mode | Example: `claude-opus-4-8` on Anthropic API, `us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8` on Bedrock |\n| `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL` | Model ID for `sonnet` alias and `opusplan` in execution mode | Also used for `opusplan` when not in plan mode |\n| `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL` | Model ID for `haiku` alias and background functionality | Replaces the deprecated `ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL` |\n| `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_FABLE_MODEL` | Model ID for `fable` alias and automatic model fallback recognition | Used for Fable 5 on third-party providers |\n| `ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL` | **DEPRECATED** - Haiku-class model for background tasks | Use `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL` instead |\n\n### Custom Model Display (for gateway/proxy deployments)\n\n| Variable | Purpose | Notes |\n|----------|---------|-------|\n| `ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_MODEL_OPTION` | Model ID to add as custom entry in `/model` picker | For gateway-specific models not listed by default |\n| `ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_MODEL_OPTION_NAME` | Display name for custom model in picker | Defaults to model ID if not set |\n| `ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_MODEL_OPTION_DESCRIPTION` | Display description for custom model | Defaults to \"Custom model ()\" if not set |\n| `ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_MODEL_OPTION_SUPPORTED_CAPABILITIES` | Comma-separated capabilities: `effort`, `xhigh_effort`, `max_effort`, `thinking`, `adaptive_thinking`, `interleaved_thinking` | Tells Claude Code which features the model supports |\n\n### Capability Declaration for Pinned Models (Bedrock/Vertex/Foundry)\n\nFor each `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL` variable, you can add suffixes:\n\n| Variable Suffix | Purpose |\n|-----------------|---------|\n| `_NAME` | Display name in `/model` picker (e.g., `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL_NAME`) |\n| `_DESCRIPTION` | Display description (e.g., `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL_DESCRIPTION`) |\n| `_SUPPORTED_CAPABILITIES` | Declare which features the model supports |\n\n### Provider-Specific Routing\n\n| Variable | Purpose | Notes |\n|----------|---------|-------|\n| `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK` | Use Amazon Bedrock | Set to `1` to enable |\n| `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX` | Use Google Vertex AI | Set to `1` to enable |\n| `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_FOUNDRY` | Use Microsoft Foundry | Set to `1` to enable |\n| `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_MANTLE` | Use Bedrock Mantle endpoint | Set to `1` to enable |\n| `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_ANTHROPIC_AWS` | Use Claude Platform on AWS | Set to `1` to enable |\n| `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` | **Out of scope for your use case** - you're already setting this in your proxy | This controls API endpoint routing, not model selection |\n\n### Extended Context\n\n| Variable | Purpose | Notes |\n|----------|---------|-------|\n| `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_1M_CONTEXT` | Disable 1M context window support | Set to `1` to disable. Removes 1M variants from picker |\n\n### Fast Mode (Opus-specific)\n\n| Variable | Purpose | Notes |\n|----------|---------|-------|\n| `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_FAST_MODE` | Disable fast mode entirely | Set to `1` to disable |\n| `CLAUDE_CODE_OPUS_4_6_FAST_MODE_OVERRIDE` | **REMOVED in v2.1.160** - was a no-op | Use `/model` to select Opus 4.6, then `/fast on` |\n\n### Model Override Precedence (highest to lowest)\n\n1. **CLI flag**: `--model <alias_or_id>`\n2. **In-session command**: `/model <alias_or_id>` (saves to user settings)\n3. **Environment variable**: `ANTHROPIC_MODEL`\n4. **Settings file**: `model` field in settings.json\n5. **Default model**: Based on account type (Opus 4.8 for Max/Team/Enterprise/API, Sonnet 4.6 for Pro, Sonnet 4.5 for Bedrock/Vertex/Foundry)\n\n### Subagent Model Resolution\n\nWhen a subagent is invoked, Claude Code resolves its model in this order:\n\n1. `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL` environment variable (if set)\n2. Per-invocation `model` parameter passed to Agent tool\n3. Subagent definition's `model` frontmatter field\n4. Main conversation's model\n\n### For Your Reverse Proxy (claude-tap-plus)\n\nSince you're injecting env vars to route by model, you'll want to set:\n\n- **`ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL`** - to your Opus model ID (proxy will see `opus` → rewrites to your ID)\n- **`ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL`** - to your Sonnet model ID (proxy will see `sonnet` → rewrites to your ID)\n- **`ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL`** - to your Haiku model ID (proxy will see `haiku` → rewrites to your ID)\n- **`ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_FABLE_MODEL`** - to your Fable model ID (proxy will see `fable` → rewrites to your ID)\n- **`CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL`** - if you want subagents to use a specific model (or set to `inherit` to use main conversation model)\n\n### Extended Context Suffix\n\nFor 1M context on third-party providers, append `[1m]` to the model ID:\n\n```bash\nexport ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL='claude-opus-4-8[1m]'\nexport ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL='claude-sonnet-4-6[1m]'\n```\n\nClaude Code strips the suffix before sending to the provider.\n\n**Documentation sources:**\n- https://code.claude.com/docs/en/model-config.md\n- https://code.claude.com/docs/en/env-vars.md\n- https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents.md"}],"totalDurationMs":35009,"totalTokens":341192,"totalToolUseCount":0,"usage":{"input_tokens":156578,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":182848,"output_tokens":1766,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"tool_use_id":"call_4c70c0a1c7a74a9b93202fff","duration_ms":35011}
